      "text": "justice of God did also divide the wicked, 1 Ne. 15:30. greatness and the justice of our God, 2 Ne. 9:17. the atonement satisfieth the demands of his justice, 2 Ne. 9:26. he denieth none that come unto him, black and white, 2 Ne. 26:33. he counseleth in wisdom, and in justice, Jacob 4:10. justice cannot be denied, Jacob 6:10. demands of divine justice do awaken his immortal soul, Mosiah 2:38. justice, and mercy of him who created, Mosiah 5:15. confess before God that his judgments are just, Mosiah 16:1. works of justice could not be destroyed, Alma 12:32. justice of God that men should be judged according to their works, Alma 41:3. atonement … to appease the demands of justice, Alma 42:15. do ye suppose that mercy can rob justice, Alma 42:25. ye should deny the justice of God no more, Alma 42:30. justice and judgment may come upon the wicked, Alma 60:13. according to the … justice … which is in Christ, 3 Ne. 26:5. to be judged of their works, whether they be good, 3 Ne. 27:14. sword of his justice is in his right hand, 3 Ne. 29:4.",
